.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-import 1  "tapectl-import " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-import \- Import a pre\-existing volume into the database
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl import\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-label\fR> [\fB\-\-backend\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] <\fB\-\-generation\fR> [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-capacity\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import a pre\-existing volume into the database
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
Volume label
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR [default: lto]
Backend type
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Media generation (e.g., LTO\-6, LTO\-7, LTO\-7\-M8, LTO\-8)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-capacity\fR \fI<CAPACITY>\fR
Capacity (e.g., "2500G"). Decimal, as printed on the cartridge (K=10^3 ... T=10^12; ADR\-0012) — not the binary unit `slice_size`/`enospc_buffer` use.

Defaults to the generation table\*(Aqs native capacity for `\-\-generation` when omitted (ADR\-0010, decision 3).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Which configured drive this volume belongs to, by its device path (ADR\-0010). Only needed when more than one `[[backends.lto]]` is configured — with one drive, or none, the behaviour is unchanged. Resolved leniently: this command only writes a catalog row and never touches the device, so a path no backend claims is not an error (issue #151)
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fI<NOTES>\fR
Notes
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
